Network: private addresses need a literal-IP grant.

A granted host name may only connect to public addresses once resolved, so
DNS rebinding or a name pointed at 169.254.169.254 cannot reach the local
network. A literal IP grant reaches exactly that IP; `localhost` reaches
loopback. Covers net.connect, WebSocket and fetch (through a reqwest
resolver); a proxy resolves on its own side and is not covered.

